From: EGoTouchRev Linux maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] dmaengine: qcom: gpi: clear peripheral configuration after freeing

gpi_free_chan_resources() frees the per-channel configuration but leaves the
pointer populated. A subsequent user of the same DMA channel passes that
freed pointer to krealloc() in gpi_peripheral_config(). This is invalid even
when both clients request the same configuration size and may overwrite an
unrelated object that has since acquired the allocation.

Clear the pointer after freeing it so that a new channel user receives a
new configuration allocation.

Observed while unloading/reloading the Gaokun GENI SPI controller. The first
eight bytes of its SPI configuration, 01 00 01 01 01 04 00 00, subsequently
appeared as corrupted pointers in DRM and memcg Oops reports.

--- a/drivers/dma/qcom/gpi.c
+++ b/drivers/dma/qcom/gpi.c
@@ -2011,6 +2011,7 @@ static void gpi_free_chan_resources(struct dma_chan *chan)
 	gpi_free_ring(&gchan->ch_ring, gpii);
 	vchan_free_chan_resources(&gchan->vc);
 	kfree(gchan->config);
+	gchan->config = NULL;
 
 	write_lock_irq(&gpii->pm_lock);
 	gchan->pm_state = DISABLE_STATE;
